== Blood Donation Machine ==
{{infobox entity
 | name    = Blood Donation Machine
 | variant = 2
}}

Bumping into the '''Blood Donation Machine''' will damage Isaac. The machine will then pay out with 1-2 of any type of {{e|Penny|text=Coin}} (only 1 in Hard Mode) or, rarely, {{t|Child's Heart}}. Every donation has a 6.66% chance of causing the Blood Donation Machine to explode, giving either a {{i|Blood Bag}} or an {{i|IV Bag}}. Alternatively, it can be destroyed with a {{e|Bomb}}, which will cause it to drop several coin or heart [[pickup]]s.

=== Notes ===
* On the floors before {{s|Womb}}, the Machine will take a half-heart of health from each use. From Womb and onward, the Blood Donation Machine will take one full heart instead.
* Once a Blood Donation Machine has given {{I|IV Bag}}, future Blood Donation Machines will never pay out with it again for the rest of the run unless Blood Bag has not been unlocked yet.
* It is possible for any number of {{i|Blood Bag}}s to appear in the same run.
* {{i|Holy Mantle}} does not prevent damage from a Blood Donation Machine.
* [[Invulnerability]] and [[shield]]s can be used to prevent damage from it.
* {{dlc|nr}} The Machine will accept {{e|Eternal Heart}}s first, then {{e|Red Heart}}s. When Isaac's health is at half a heart (or a full heart in {{s|Womb}} and beyond), the Machine will drain {{e|Soul Heart}}s and {{e|Black Heart}}s instead.
* {{dlc|nr}} While the Machine takes Red Hearts before Soul Hearts or Black Hearts, using a Blood Donation Machine will trigger {{i|Scapular}} once Isaac is at half a heart. Leaving the room afterward and then reentering resets Scapular, allowing for further donations using Soul Hearts. Repeating this process after every Scapular activation allows Isaac to collect coins from the Blood Donation Machine until it breaks.
* {{dlc|nr}} With {{i|Isaac's Heart}}, the Machine can be used without taking any damage.
* {{dlc|nr}} Invincibility frames can be used to activate a Blood Donation Machine for free.
* {{dlc|r}} Blood Donation Machines will drain Isaac's last half Red Heart before draining Soul Hearts.
* {{dlc|r}} The Machine will ignore Eternal Hearts if Isaac has any other heart type, unless it would deal fatal damage.
* {{dlc|r}} If Isaac has Red and {{e|Rotten Heart|n}}s, the Machine will take Red Hearts before taking Rotten Hearts.
* {{dlc|r}} When using {{C|Keeper}} or {{c|Tainted Keeper}}, the Machine has a chance to pay out with no coins, preventing abuse.
{{clear}}

== Shop Restock Machine ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc     = a
 | name    = Shop Restock Machine
 | variant = 10
}}

The '''Shop Restock Machine''' commonly appears in {{r|Shop}}s in [[Greed Mode]], and rarely in {{r|Arcade}}s, {{r|Black Market}}s, {{r|Crawl Space}}s, {{r|I AM ERROR}} rooms, {{r|Secret Room}}s, and {{r|Treasure Room}}s outside of Greed Mode. Shop Restock Machines also have a chance to spawn in {{r|Shop}}s outside of Greed Mode, replacing the Donation Machine.

In {{r|Shop}}s and {{r|Black Market}}s, each activation will cause the following effects:
* Rerolls every [[item]] and [[pickup]] for sale.
* Refills all empty Shop slots.
* Item pedestals in the room that are not for sale will not be rerolled.
The chance for the Shop to be restocked increases as more coins are inserted.

In all other rooms, the Shop Restock Machine will reroll any items present after donating enough pennies or blowing it up. It will not generate new items to replace the taken ones. It will reroll all items in the room even if they were not originally present (e.g. items from {{m|Beggar}}s).

Shop Restock Machines can break after the fourth guaranteed reroll with a 50% chance for every subsequent reroll that should've been successful. This will cause them to drop a small number of coins.

{{dlc|r}} Bombing a Shop Restock Machine breaks it immediately. 
* {{dlc|nr+}} When a Shop Restock Machine explodes, either through bombing or extended use, it has a chance to rapidly reroll all items a few times. With timing, any item seen briefly during the rapid reroll process can be picked up, similar to acquiring items from {{i|Glitched Crown|n}}. Saving and quitting in the middle of the reroll process will cause the items to stop rerolling upon re-entering the game.

{{dlc|r}} Restocking the shop in the [[Mirrored World|Mirrored world]] will make items appear in the mirrored shop. The normal shop will not be rerolled, and subsequent rerolls will not match those of the mirrored shop.
{{clear}}

== Mom's Dressing Table ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc     = a+
 | name    = Mom's Dressing Table
 | variant = 12
}}

'''Mom's Dressing Table''' is an object added in [[Booster Pack#2]]. {{dlc+|nr}} If Isaac has more than 8 items, it has a 50% chance of appearing in the starting room of a floor.{{dlc-}} {{dlc+|r}} Mom's Dressing Tables have a high chance to spawn in {{r|Clean Bedroom}}s and {{r|Dirty Bedroom}}s.{{dlc-}}

If Isaac bumps into Mom's Dressing Table, his appearance will be randomly changed such that only a few of his items are displayed.

Hitting Mom's Dressing Table with an explosive will cause it to break and drop 1-4 [[pills]]. There is a 1% chance to spawn one of the following items instead: {{i|Mom's Underwear}}, {{i|Mom's Heels}}, {{i|Mom's Lipstick}}, {{i|Mom's Bra}}, {{i|Mom's Pad}}, {{i|Mom's Eyeshadow}}, {{i|Mom's Contacts}}, {{i|Mom's Wig}}, {{i|Mom's Perfume}} or {{i|Mom's Pearls}}. Items that have already been generated and/or collected can be spawned again in this manner.
{{clear}}

== Crane Game ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc         = r
 | name        = Crane Game
 | variant     = 16
 | unlocked by = Crane Game
}}

The '''Crane Game''' can appear in {{r|Arcade}}s and rarely in normal rooms after being unlocked. It can also appear in the Greed Mode Shop, replacing the Shop Restock Machine. The Machine contains one visible [[item]]; after the Machine pays out, another one will be displayed. A grapple is above the items. The Machine pays out prizes from the {{ip|Crane Game|text=Crane Game item pool}}.

Bumping into the Machine consumes 5 cents and activates the grapple, which will attempt to grab the item in the center. If it succeeds, the item will be taken out of the Machine and appear on a pedestal.

There is a 25% chance for the Machine to pay out, so the probability of the Machine paying out after at most <math>N</math> tries is <math>1-(3/4)^N</math>. The Machine explodes after giving 3 prizes.

Alternatively, it can be destroyed with a {{e|Bomb}}, which will cause it to drop several [[pickups]].
* if the Machine is destroyed during its payout animation, it will still give the item.

The Crane Game won't change the reward item once it has been displayed, even if it was picked up elsewhere in the level. The same item can even be paid out twice in a row: the next item is determined before the first one is fully spawned, and at that point the reward is locked.

Once all items in the Crane Game item pool have been picked up, the Crane Game will only dispense {{I|Buddy in a Box}}.

Leaving the room while the animation is still playing after winning will cause the reward to not spawn.

{{dlc|r+}} Crane Games have a 1% chance to appear from a {{p|X - Wheel of Fortune}} card.

Will be replaced with a {{m|Slot Machine}} if not unlocked.
{{clear}}

== Confessional ==
{{infobox entity
 | dlc         = r
 | name        = Confessional
 | variant     = 17
 | unlocked by = Confessional
}}

The '''Confessional''' damages Isaac with the same rules as the '''Blood Donation Machine''' in exchange for various rewards. It can be found in {{r|Super Secret Room}}s or {{r|Angel Room}}s, but can rarely be found in normal rooms.

The Confessional has a 30% chance on Normal Mode and 25% chance on [[Hard Mode]] to pay out. This is increased by 1.5× if Isaac has {{i|Lucky Foot}}.

The following are the rewards and are evaluated in the order they are listed.

* 5% chance to explode.
* 3.3% chance to explode giving an {{ip|Angel Room|text=Angel Room item}}.
** If a [[Deal with the Devil]] has been made this run, it will instead give {{i|Redemption}}.
* Removes a [[Health#Broken Hearts|Broken Heart]], if Isaac has one.
* 46.875% chance to receive a {{e|Soul Heart}}. Reduced to 9.375% if Isaac has {{T|Daemon's Tail}}.
* 3.125% chance to receive an {{e|Eternal Heart}}. Reduced to 0.125% if Isaac has {{T|Daemon's Tail}}.
* "You Feel Blessed!": Removes an active [[curse]]. For the current floor, increases {{r|Angel Room}} chance by 10% and allows Isaac to find an Angel Room even if he already made a Deal with the Devil. This effect stacks additively, going up to a 100% Angel Room chance at 10 activations.
** If Isaac hasn't seen any {{r|Devil Room}}s or {{r|Angel Room}}s before and the fortune is activated once, the deal on that floor is guaranteed to be an Angel Room.

Alternatively, it can be destroyed with a {{e|Bomb}}, which will cause it to drop [[pickups]], with a chance to drop [[trinkets]] as well. Despite its appearance, destroying a Confessional does not affect {{r|Angel Room}} or {{r|Devil Room}} chance.

Will be replaced with a {{e|Soul Heart}} if not unlocked.

=== Notes ===
* [[Invulnerability]] and [[shield]]s can be used to prevent damage from it.
